BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Board and the Empire: Satyajit Ray’s Shatranj Ke Khilari
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260905T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260905T140000
UID:the-board-and-the-empire-satyajit-ray-s-shatranj-ke-khilari-2026-09-05
 t14-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/08
 /SKK_Still_01-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Presented in conjunction with Game On! and programmed by film 
 scholar\, author\, critic\, and curator Narendra Pachkhédé\, this screen
 ing of Satyajit Ray’s Shatranj Ke Khilari ( The Chess Players ) explores
  chess as a cultural form and a lens on power\, strategy\, and political i
 naction.\n\nA brief introduction by Pachkédé will connect the film to th
 ree works in the exhibition. A 12th-century Iranian chess set\, the Shahna
 meh folio “Buzurjmihr Masters the Indian Game of Chess\,” and Yoko Ono
 ’s Play It By Trust . Together\, they trace chess from its material and 
 courtly histories to its modern role as a space of cooperation.\n\nThe scr
 eening will be followed by a conversation between Bita Pourvash\, curator 
 of Game On! \, and Narendra Pachkhédé\, film scholar\, author\, critic\,
  and curator\, exploring what games reveal about conflict\, responsibility
 \, and historical change.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/shatranj-ke-khila/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
