BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Sacred in Song: Voices from Kurdistan
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260913T140000
UID:the-sacred-in-song-voices-from-kurdistan-2026-09-13t14-00-00-04-00@aga
 khanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/08
 /Song-of-god-Main-Still-frame-2-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?r
 esize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Experience an evening of film and live music exploring the rel
 ationship between sound and spirituality\, while celebrating the musical h
 eritage of Kurdistan and the broader Iranian cultural sphere.\n\nFirst\, e
 njoy a film screening of Song of God \, an intimate documentary by Iranian
 -Canadian filmmaker Aref Mohammadi. Following the screening\, the Andalib 
 Ensemble takes the stage for a special performance bringing Kurdish maqams
  and regional traditions from across Kurdistan into dialogue with Persian 
 classical music.\n\nFilm duration: 60 minutes
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/the-sacred-in-song/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Warren Senders: Entering the World of Raga
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260919T193000
UID:warren-senders-entering-the-world-of-raga-2026-09-19t19-30-00-04-00@ag
 akhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/09
 /Warren-Senders-aspect-ratio-1600-1000.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Enjoy an evening of soulful vocals\, intricate rhythms\, and m
 usical exchange at the Aga Khan Museum.\n\nBringing together three accompl
 ished artists of classical music\, this vocal recital celebrates the expre
 ssive depth of raga through voice\, harmonium\, and tabla. Acclaimed khaya
 l vocalist Warren brings decades of experience with Indian\, Western\, Afr
 ican\, and African-American music. He is joined by harmonium accompanist H
 ardeep and distinguished tabla artist Kiran.\n\nTogether\, the musicians c
 reate an intimate and dynamic musical exchange\, balancing the meditative 
 qualities of raga with the energy of rhythmic interplay and improvisation.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/warren-senders-vocal-recital/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
