BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Couchiching Annual Conference 2026
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T083000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261007T190000
UID:couchiching-annual-conference-2026-2026-10-07t08-30-00-04-00@agakhanmu
 seum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/07
 /1710-AKM-Orhan-Pamuk-7110-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize
 =1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:The Couchiching Conference\, co-hosted by the Canadian Interna
 tional Council (CIC) and the Aga Khan Museum\, aims to foster an inclusive
  dialogue on the evolving role of diplomacy on the international stage. Th
 is event will provide a platform for citizens\, journalists\, academics\, 
 and students to engage in meaningful discussions on international affairs\
 , reflecting our shared mission to give Canadians a voice in global matter
 s.\n\nCanada is entering a period defined by geopolitical uncertainty\, te
 chnological disruption\, and shifting alliances. This year’s Couchiching
  Conference will bring together policymakers\, industry leaders\, and glob
 al thinkers to explore the choices shaping Canada’s role in the world.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/couchiching-annual-conference-2026/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Poems of Consumption by H. Sinno
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261010T200000
UID:poems-of-consumption-by-h-sinno-2026-10-10t20-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseu
 m.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/08
 /preferred-HSINNO-X-REFORM-THE-FUNK-03-2-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-1-s
 caled.jpg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:H.Sinno’s acclaimed performance\, Poems of Consumption \, re
 imagines consumer culture through music\, poetry\, and immersive visuals.\
 n\nPart concert\, part multimedia performance\, and part poetic meditation
 \, Poems of Consumption explores the emotional contradictions of modern li
 fe through songs built from an unexpected source: Amazon customer reviews 
 transformed into poetry. Partially inspired by Mark Fisher’s Capitalist 
 Realism \, Poems of Consumption is a song cycle covering themes like ennui
 \, surveillance capitalism\, heartbreak\, boycotts\, and orientalism\, wit
 h compositions that juxtapose harsh electronica with the whimsy of a strin
 g quartet.\n\nOriginally commissioned by London’s Barbican Centre and Sh
 ubbak Festival\, the production has been praised for its fearless artistic
  vision and emotional honesty\, bringing together experimental music\, the
 atre\, and literature into a deeply personal live experience.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/poems-of-consumption/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ishq Ke Saat Muqaam
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261016T200000
UID:ishq-ke-saat-muqaam-2026-10-16t20-00-00-04-00@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/08
 /ISM_AKM.png?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Ishq Ke Saat Muqaam (The Seven Stages of Love) returns with a 
 renewed artistic vision\, bringing together poetry\, music\, dance\, and s
 torytelling to explore one of humanity’s oldest and most profound questi
 ons: what does it mean to love?\n\nWritten and directed by Nishar Mansuri\
 , the production is inspired by the Sufi understanding of ishq as a path o
 f transformation. Through seven interconnected stages\, the work moves fro
 m human longing to self-discovery\, devotion\, and surrender\, inviting au
 diences into a journey that is both deeply personal and universal.\n\nFeat
 uring the poetry of Rumi\, Amir Khusrau\, Kabir\, Bulleh Shah\, Hafez\, Fa
 riduddin Attar\, Sultan Bahu\, and other mystic voices\, the production re
 imagines centuries of mystical thought through contemporary performance. T
 heir words become the foundation for an experience that transcends borders
 \, languages\, and faith traditions\, inviting audiences to reflect on lov
 e as a force that connects us all.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/ishq-ke-saat-muqaam/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
