BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fasayfisa’: Introduction to Mosaic Workshop
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261017
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261026
UID:fasayfisa-introduction-to-mosaic-workshop-2026-10-17@agakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/09
 /Mosaic-Coster-Shirin-Divanbeigi4-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg
 ?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Discover the beauty and meaning behind Fasayfisa’ — an Ara
 bic term for small\, colourful pieces of marble or stone arranged side by 
 side to form a unified design.\n\nThrough this hands-on workshop\, partici
 pants will create a small ornament using vibrant glass tiles\, inspired by
  the intricate patterns found in Islamic art and architecture. Drawing fro
 m examples in the Aga Khan Museum Collections\, explore how these repeatin
 g designs embody harmony\, balance\, and creativity\, a tradition that has
  flourished for centuries.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-ihm-fasayfisa-mosaic-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Water Marbling Bookmarks Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T150000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20261024T150000
UID:water-marbling-bookmarks-workshop-2026-10-24t15-00-00-04-00@agakhanmus
 eum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/09
 /Water-Marbling-Workshop_Bookmarks_MadalinaRaduta1-scaled-aspect-ratio-160
 0-1000-scaled.jpeg?resize=1584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:Immerse yourself in the mesmerizing world of water marbling 
 — an ancient technique of floating pigments on water and transferring th
 em onto paper to create intricate\, fluid designs.\n\nPracticed for centur
 ies across the Islamic world\, particularly in regions such as Türkiye\, 
 Iran\, and the Indian subcontinent\, water marbling has been used to adorn
  calligraphy\, manuscripts\, and decorative papers. In this introductory w
 orkshop\, you will explore its rich history and cultural significance whil
 e mastering traditional tools and methods to produce a variety of classic 
 patterns. Guided step-by-step\, you will create between five and eight uni
 que marbled bookmarks to take home — each a one-of-a-kind reflection of 
 colour\, movement\, and your own creative expression.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-ihm-water-marbling-workshop/
X-SOURCE:Aga Khan Museum
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:2026 Duende International Flamenco Festival: Masterclasses
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261118
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261123
UID:2026-duende-international-flamenco-festival-masterclasses-2026-11-18@a
 gakhanmuseum.org
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://images.agakhanmuseum.org/uploads/2026/06
 /25.11_AK_Duende_3__5167-scaled-aspect-ratio-1600-1000-scaled.jpg?resize=1
 584%2C990&gravity
DESCRIPTION:This special series of masterclasses offers dancers a rare opp
 ortunity to learn with three extraordinary flamenco artists\, Óscar de lo
 s Reyes\, Carmen Talegona\, and El Yiyo.\n\nEach workshop offers participa
 nts a deeper understanding of the art form’s power\, precision\, musical
 ity\, and emotional truth. The three artists brings a distinct voice\, lin
 eage\, and approach\, guiding dancers toward greater technical clarity\, e
 xpressive range\, and connection to rhythm\, structure\, and cante. Togeth
 er\, these masterclasses create a rich encounter with flamenco as a living
 \, evolving art form — one that honours tradition while continuing to mo
 ve boldly into the future.\n\nOpen to intermediate\, advanced\, and profes
 sional-level dancers\, the workshops offer an inspiring environment for gr
 owth\, exchange\, and artistic discovery.
LOCATION:Aga Khan Museum\, 77 Wynford Drive\, Toronto\, ON M3C 1K1
URL:https://agakhanmuseum.org/whats-on/2026-duende-international-flamenco-
 festival-masterclasses/
